From: ms178 <ms178@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 22:43:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] =?UTF-8?q?aarch64:=20three=20peephole=20passes=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20zext-mask=20fold,=20ANDS/TST=20fusion,=20dead=20pre?=
 =?UTF-8?q?-ret=20moves?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Census-vs-GCC gaps on AArch64 (xarch probes): every widening cast emitted
a redundant `and x0, x0, #0xff/#0xffff` re-mask; every `(a & b) != 0`
bool gate burned a `cmp` after the `and`; return staging left dead
`mov xN, xS` writes (bool_gate shaped: 15 -> 12 insns; load_cmp loop
loses one instruction per iteration).

  * eliminate_redundant_zext_and: forward width-bound tracking
    (value < 2^w) per basic-block region. Producers: zero-extending
    loads (ldrb/ldurb/ldarb/... = 8, ldrh family = 16), previous masks,
    unshifted immediates, ubfx #0,#w, uxtb/uxth, register moves (w-form
    clamps to 32); everything else widens to its form (w-write = 32,
    x-write/calls/labels = no info). `and d, s, #mask` with
    bound(s) <= mask width rewrites to `mov d, s` (value-identical,
    flags untouched). Soundness pins: the source bound is captured
    BEFORE the destination update (in-place `and x0, x0, #mask` used to
    validate itself against its own post-mask bound and delete a
    semantically required truncation after `sxth` — caught by
    cast_chain_fold/sqlite_yy_shift differential); shifted `movz`
    rewrites the register so the old bound is dropped, not kept;
    ands sets flags and is never rewritten.
  * fuse_and_cmp_zero: `and wA, wB, C; cmp wA, #0` + N/Z/V-only
    consumer (eq/ne/mi/pl/ge/lt/gt/le/vs/vc) -> `ands wA, wB, C`, cmp
    deleted. Exactness: N/Z identical (same value), V=0 on both sides;
    C differs (shifter carry vs borrow-never), so C-consuming
    conditions are excluded. The operand tail is preserved verbatim
    (shifted-register forms). CCC_NO_AND_TST_FUSION kill switch.
  * eliminate_dead_pre_ret_moves: `mov xD, xS` (dst in 1..=28 — x0 is
    the return register and x30 is read by ret) with no read of xD
    before the ret is dead and deleted; a pure redefinition also proves
    death. Any ambiguous mention aborts.

Validation: lib 1282/0/6 (9 new unit tests incl. the self-validating
mask regression); ARM 378/30/75 = baseline with all passes active;
x86 536/5 unchanged; f128 battery (softfloat, global_carrier,
scalar_fp_builtins, vex_move_false_dep, param_home_order,
preserves_gp_param, glibc_f128_casts/builtins) all green on qemu.
