From fd4bfd9bc4fd4602b7a8f5584b276c3705200d67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ms178 <ms178@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 23:24:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] aarch64: fix trampoline encodings; executable GNU_STACK
 in builtin linker
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Address-taken nested functions segfaulted under every call shape
(nested_functions rc=139; two independent defects):

1. Trampoline literal encodings were off by one word. The imm19 of an
   AArch64 LDR (literal) is the byte offset / 4, but both hand-coded
   words were computed from the WORD offset, so `ldr x18` read the
   literal-slot padding at +12 (a nop) and `ldr x17` read half the
   static-chain doubleword at +20 instead of the function pointer at
   +24. Every trampoline call jumped through garbage.

   The two data words live at +16/+24 in a 32-byte, 16-aligned buffer
   (ir/lowering/nested_functions.rs allocates 32B@16; unchanged), so the
   correct encodings are 0x5800_0092 (ldr x18, [pc+#16], imm19=4) and
   0x5800_00B1 (ldr x17, [pc+#20], imm19=5). GCC 14.2 emits the same
   x17 word byte-for-byte inside its 40-byte, BTI-marked trampoline
   (`bti c; ldr x17,[pc+#20]; ldr x18,[pc+#24]; br`, data +24/+32).
   `bti c` is deliberately still omitted: lccc emits no
   .note.gnu.property yet, so a BTI instruction would itself fault once
   BTI is enabled kernel- or toolchain-side. Revisit together with BTI
   support. Module doc rewritten with the derived encodings and the
   GCC reference layout.

2. The builtin AArch64 linker always emitted PT_GNU_STACK as RW.
   lccc's backend marks `.note.GNU-stack,"x"` for units that initialise
   trampolines, and binutils ORs all input notes into the final
   PT_GNU_STACK flags; the hand-written emitters must mirror that.
   Without PF_X, the kernel refuses to execute the trampoline and the
   first indirect nested call dies with SIGSEGV even with correct
   words. All three emitters (emit_static, emit_dynamic, emit_shared)
   now scan every input's sections and set PF_X when any
   `.note.GNU-stack` carries SHF_EXECINSTR — the exact policy
   i686/linker/emit.rs (and shared.rs) already implements.

Verified: nested_functions rc=0 under qemu-aarch64 (was rc=139);
trampoline words printed by a probe are 58000092 580000b1 d61f0220
d503201f with f0(f2,&i)=8, i=7 (GCC 14.2 agrees); readelf shows RWE
GNU_STACK only for trampoline units; full ARM differential corpus
379 passed / 93 failed vs 377/95 baseline (fail set otherwise
identical); cargo test --lib 1282 passed under -D warnings.
