From c5623a7691149f25e18b9c45580191f2b2c409d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ms178 <ms178@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 23:24:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] loop_unroll: thread loop-carried phis through partial
 unroll
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

do_unroll rethreaded only the IV phi through the exit-check chain. Any
OTHER header phi — a reduction accumulator, a marching pointer — kept
reading its pre-iteration value inside every clone: the clone's update
became dead, DCE deleted it, and the loop silently skipped k-1 of every
k elements whenever the runtime trip count hit the unrolled fast path.
lea_sib_fold printed "45 18" instead of "45 25": the vectorized body
consumed 4 elements, the remainder loop ran under a 4x partial unroll,
and the final element's add fed a phi that never saw it.

Three coupled fixes in do_unroll:

1. Carried-phi threading. Collect every non-IV header phi whose
   latch-incoming operand is a value L0 (the original body's update).
   Clone j reads prev_j = L0 renamed by clone j-1's value map (L0
   itself for clone 0); the header phi's latch incoming becomes the
   last clone's copy (step 4b). Substitution uses the canonical
   subst_value_with_operand AFTER the clone's own vmap rename —
   substituting before would let the vmap re-rename the injected value
   onto the clone's own id, producing self-referencing adds.

2. Exit-edge updates (step 5). For exit-block phis fed by the header,
   the value on each NEW exit-check edge is the latch-incoming operand
   renamed by the last executed clone's map — NOT the header-edge
   operand, which on the path preheader->header->body->exit_check is
   still the preheader value because the phi's update rides the latch
   edge the early exit never takes. The IV uses the check block's own
   prev+step result.

3. Exit phis for lowered loops (step 5b). When the exit block has NO
   header-fed phi for the IV or a carried value (later passes may have
   already lowered loop phis to explicit edge copies), readers after
   the loop still use the header phi's dest SSA name and would observe
   the stale preheader value on the new edges. Insert a proper exit
   phi — fresh dest, the header phi itself on the header edge, the
